    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-blue-600">12th board cut off calculator</span>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-2xl">
          How to Calculate Your Cut Off From 12th Board Marks: Worked Examples
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.7] text-slate-700">
          Most students search for a 12th cut off calculator expecting a single answer. There is no single
          answer &mdash; there is one answer per state. The four sections below take the same three marks,
          <strong class="font-semibold text-slate-900">88 in Mathematics, 76 in Physics and 81 in Chemistry</strong>,
          through four published formulas so you can see exactly where each state&rsquo;s number comes from.
          Read your own state&rsquo;s row, then enter the same marks in that calculator to confirm.
        </p>
      </div>

